course: dictionary
lesson: 4754
title: Hotspot: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «Yellowstone sits on top of a huge volcanic hotspot that feeds its geysers.» The words volcanic and geysers tell you this hotspot is a hot place deep in the Earth, not a busy place full of people.
explain: In science, a hotspot is where hot rock rises from deep in the Earth. «As the plate slides over a hotspot, a chain of volcanoes forms.» The plate moves, but the hotspot stays put, so each volcano forms in a new place, and the Hawaiian islands get older the further they are from the hotspot.
explain: Other meanings are about people and things. A tourist hotspot is a place with lots of visitors, a crime hotspot is a place with lots of crime, and a Wi-Fi hotspot lets you connect to the internet without wires. Ask: what is the topic of the text? The topic tells you which meaning to choose.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If «hot rock rising from deep in the Earth» fits the sentence, you have the right meaning.
fact: A hotspot is a place where there is a lot of a certain activity, such as a tourist hotspot.
fact: A Wi-Fi hotspot is a place or device that lets you connect to the internet without wires.
fact: In science, a hotspot is a place where hot rock rises from deep in the Earth, making volcanoes, as under Hawaii or Iceland.
fact: A biodiversity hotspot is an area with very many different kinds of plants and animals that are in danger.
fact: The same word can have different meanings in different subjects, so the context tells you which one is meant.
exercise: «As the plate slides over a hotspot, a chain of volcanoes forms.» In this sentence, what is a hotspot? | Place where an illness spreads fast | Public place with free Wi-Fi | *Place where hot rock rises from deep in the Earth | Crowded place with lots of visitors
exercise: Mum says, «Our tablet cannot get online here, so we will use the hotspot on my phone.» What does hotspot mean here? | A place where hot rock rises | A place where lots of people shop | An area with many endangered animals | *A device that lets you connect to the internet without wires
exercise: «Rainforests are biodiversity hotspots, full of plants and animals that are in danger.» What does biodiversity hotspot suggest? | *An area with very many kinds of plants and animals that are in danger | A very hot, dry desert | A place with only one kind of plant | A busy shopping centre
test: «Hawaii's islands get older the further they are from the hotspot.» What is the hotspot in this sentence? | A pool of warm water near the surface | *The place where hot rock rises from deep in the Earth | A place where lots of tourists go | A Wi-Fi device for the internet
test: Jayden says a crime hotspot is a place on fire. What does it mean? | *A place with a lot of crime | A place where the Earth is hot | A place with a fire lit by police | A place where it is very hot
exam: «Some volcanoes, like Hawaii's, sit over a hotspot in the middle of a plate.» Which meaning of hotspot fits? | Place with lots of tourists | Wi-Fi device | Area with endangered animals | *Place where hot rock rises from deep in the Earth
